    "content": "# APPLICATION FOR APPROVAL OF SEMINAR TOPIC\n### Course Code: MSCS-4-04 | Course: Seminar (M.Sc. Computer Science, Semester-IV)\n\n**To:**  \nThe Course Coordinator,  \nDepartment of Computer Science & Applications,  \nJagat Guru Nanak Dev Punjab State Open University (JGND PSOU),  \nC/28, The Lower Mall, Patiala - 147001, Punjab.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Student Particulars\n\n* **Name of the Student**: `Sumit Singh`\n* **Roll Number / Enrollment No.**: `PSOU/MSCS/2026/042`\n* **Program**: Master of Science in Computer Science — M.Sc. (CS)\n* **Semester / Academic Cycle**: Semester-IV (Final Semester) / `July 2024 - 2026 Cycle`\n* **Study Centre Code / Name**: `JGND PSOU Regional Centre, Patiala`\n* **Mobile Number / Email**: `[Student Contact & Email]`\n\n---\n\n### 2. Proposed Seminar Particulars\n\n* **Domain / Area of Research**: Distributed Systems / Advanced Web Architectures / Data Consistency\n* **Proposed Title of Seminar**:  \n  **\"Architectural Patterns for Offline-First Distributed Web Applications: Balancing Zero-Latency User Experience with Eventual Consistency\"**\n* **Target Presentation Duration**: 15–20 Minutes (with additional 5 Minutes for Discussion & Questions)\n* **Expected Length of Report**: 10–15 A4 Pages (3,000–4,500 Words)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Abstract / Significance of the Proposed Seminar Topic\n\nIn high-reliability enterprise web applications, the traditional \"thin-client / thick-server\" architecture introduces single points of failure, latency spikes, and complete operational failure during network disruptions. The emerging **\"Local-First\" and \"Offline-First\" distributed paradigm** shifts the primary operational data store directly into the client's browser runtime (via IndexedDB and local transactional storage engines), allowing instantaneous local state mutations ($< 1\\text{ms}$) while decoupling remote database writes via asynchronous background synchronization queues.\n\nThis seminar will explore:\n1. The theoretical foundations of local-first software, CAP theorem trade-offs, and distributed consensus models.\n2. Conflict resolution mechanisms, including Conflict-Free Replicated Data Types (CRDTs), vector clocks, and idempotency key queues.\n3. Modern browser-based transactional engines (IndexedDB, Dexie.js) paired with event-driven backend workers.\n4. Real-world case study implementation and empirical performance benchmarks demonstrating how offline-first architectures achieve high fault tolerance and zero-latency user experiences in mission-critical software.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Preliminary References & Literature\n1. Kleppmann, M., Wiggins, A., van Hardenberg, M., & McGranaghan, M. (2019). *\"Local-first software: you own your data, in spite of the cloud.\"* Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction (PACMHCI), Vol. 3, Issue OOPSLA.\n2. Shapiro, N., Preguiça, N., Baquero, C., & Zawirski, M. (2011). *\"Conflict-Free Replicated Data Types.\"* International Symposium on Stabilization, Safety, and Security of Distributed Systems, Springer.\n3. Brewer, E. (2012). *\"CAP twelve years later: How the 'rules' have changed.\"* Computer, IEEE, 45(2), 23-29.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Undertaking by the Candidate\n\nI hereby request approval for the above seminar topic. I undertake to submit the formal Seminar Report (10–15 A4 pages) within 30 days of topic approval and deliver the oral presentation and defense as scheduled by the university.\n\n**Date**: `15/05/2026`  \n**Place**: Patiala / `Patiala`  \n\n**Signature of Candidate**: __________________________\n\n---\n\n### 6. For Official Use Only (Course Coordinator / Seminar In-charge)\n\n* **Seminar Topic Status**: [ ] Approved  /  [ ] Modification Required  /  [ ] Rejected\n* **Seminar Supervisor / Evaluator**: ___________________________________________\n* **Scheduled Date of Presentation**: `15/05/2026`  \n* **Remarks**:  \n  ____________________________________________________________________________________  \n\n**Signature of Course Coordinator**: __________________________  \n**Date**: `15/05/2026`  \n**Department Seal**:\n"
